.el .ds Aq '
.TH geectl-checkout 1  "geectl-checkout 0.2.4" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-checkout \- Check out a package into a git working copy, under the current directory. Without a package, every package in the project, one working copy each
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl checkout\fR [\fB\-\-rev\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> [\fIPACKAGE\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Check out a package into a git working copy, under the current directory. Without a package, every package in the project, one working copy each
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-rev\fR \fI<REV>\fR
The revision to check out (a number or a source md5). The latest when omitted. Needs a package
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The OBS project
.TP
[\fIPACKAGE\fR]
The OBS package. The whole project when omitted
.SH VERSION
v0.2.4
